    {"id": "a1-capb", "type": "text", "x": 60, "y": 920, "width": 340, "height": 66, "strokeColor": "#6b7280", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "roughness": 0, "groupIds": ["A1", "lane1"], "seed": 1111, "text": "Three changes to a screen that otherwise stays put.\nchooseLevelButton() is written and uncalled, so it only has to\nbe called; Redeem badge code drops from primary to the text\nbutton; Get your code goes, its job now done at A4. The info\nbutton becomes Why SimpleX is built, exactly as the TODO in\nthe file says.", "fontSize": 9, "fontFamily": 2, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "autoResize": true, "index": "a02a"},

